# Deployment configuration AFTER remediation (verified working).
# See docs/methodology.md, finding B-1 and remediation R-1/R-2/R-3.
#
# Authentication: ECDSA P-384 certificate (classical). OpenSSL 3.0.13
# cannot serve provider-defined signature keys (ML-DSA-65, p384_mldsa65)
# because ssl_set_cert() only knows built-in key types; classical
# authentication is the working option on this OpenSSL branch.
CERT=certs/ecdsa-server.crt
KEY=certs/ecdsa-server.key
CAFILE=certs/ecdsa-ca.crt
# Key exchange: hybrid X25519MLKEM768 (unchanged — the post-quantum part
# of the handshake; ClientHello key_share 1216 bytes = X25519 32 + ML-KEM-768 ek 1184).
GROUPS=X25519MLKEM768
# Provider: oqs-provider 0.12.0 built against OPTIMIZED liboqs
# (OQS_OPT_TARGET=auto, AVX2) — ML-KEM-768 keypair/encaps/decaps 3.8-5.7x
# faster than the reference build at the liboqs layer (see outputs/).
PROVIDER_DIR=<path-to>/oqs-opt-mod
OPENSSL_CONF=configs/openssl-providers.cnf
# Session tickets (TLS 1.3 resumption) stay enabled (s_server default):
# repeat connections resume and skip the KEM + signature exchange —
# measured resumed median 14-15 ms vs full 18-19 ms.
